From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 May 2026 05:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Replace coordination_agent_recoverable ABSL_FLAG with env var

In conda-forge's systemlib build of TensorFlow the same process loads
multiple shared objects that each statically embed
xla/tsl/distributed_runtime/coordination/coordination_service_agent.cc,
which defines ABSL_FLAG(bool, coordination_agent_recoverable, ...):

  tensorflow/libtensorflow_framework.so.2   (pywrap framework)
  lib/libtensorflow_cc.so.2.21.0            (libtensorflow_cc package, loaded
                                             via the pywrap chain at import)

absl is itself a single shared library (systemlib libabsl_flags*.so), so its
FlagRegistry is process-global. Each .so runs the flag's static registrar
against that one registry, and the second registration aborts at
`import tensorflow`:

  ERROR: Flag 'coordination_agent_recoverable' was defined more than once
  but with differing types. Defined in files
  '.../coordination_service_agent.cc' and '.../coordination_service_agent.cc'.

This is the same multi-.so duplicate-registration family handled elsewhere
in this feedstock for proto descriptors, the OpRegistry (0072) and the
PlatformObjectRegistry / GPU kernel registry (0075). Unlike those, the
registry here lives in systemized absl and cannot be patched to tolerate the
duplicate. The flag also cannot be deduplicated across the two .so's: its
only read site is in this same TU, and absl identifies flag types via a
per-translation-unit FastTypeId<bool> whose address differs between the two
.so's (hence absl's "differing types" wording).

The flag is an experimental, default-false knob (its own TODO asks to move it
to config/API), read in exactly one place. Drop the ABSL_FLAG and read the
override from the TF_COORDINATION_AGENT_RECOVERABLE environment variable
instead, parsed once. The programmatic `recoverable` parameter is unchanged,
and operators keep a global override via the env var without any absl flag
registration.
---
--- a/third_party/xla/xla/tsl/distributed_runtime/coordination/coordination_service_agent.cc
+++ b/third_party/xla/xla/tsl/distributed_runtime/coordination/coordination_service_agent.cc
@@ -30,7 +30,6 @@
 
 #include "absl/container/flat_hash_map.h"
 #include "absl/container/flat_hash_set.h"
-#include "absl/flags/flag.h"
 #include "absl/functional/bind_front.h"
 #include "absl/log/check.h"
 #include "absl/log/log.h"
@@ -53,11 +52,19 @@
 #include "xla/tsl/platform/status.h"
 #include "xla/tsl/protobuf/coordination_config.pb.h"
 #include "xla/tsl/protobuf/coordination_service.pb.h"
+#include "xla/tsl/util/env_var.h"
 
 // TODO(b/342448688): Expose via config and API instead of flag.
-ABSL_FLAG(
-    bool, coordination_agent_recoverable, false,
-    "If true, allow it to silently reconnect to the service after a restart.");
+// conda-forge: this used to be an ABSL_FLAG(coordination_agent_recoverable).
+// In the systemlib build TensorFlow is split across multiple shared objects
+// (libtensorflow_framework.so.2 and libtensorflow_cc.so.2) that each embed
+// this TU, and absl is itself a single shared library, so registering the
+// same flag from two .so's against the one process-wide absl FlagRegistry
+// aborts `import tensorflow` with "Flag 'coordination_agent_recoverable' was
+// defined more than once". A flag cannot be deduplicated across the two .so's
+// (the read site lives in this TU, and absl's per-.so FastTypeId<bool> makes
+// the registrations look like differing types), so read the override from an
+// environment variable instead of an absl flag.
 
 namespace tsl {
 using tensorflow::CoordinatedTask;
@@ -98,7 +105,13 @@
   CoordinatedTask task;
   task.set_job_name(std::string(job_name));
   task.set_task_id(task_id);
-  if (recoverable || absl::GetFlag(FLAGS_coordination_agent_recoverable)) {
+  static const bool recoverable_from_env = [] {
+    bool value = false;
+    ReadBoolFromEnvVar("TF_COORDINATION_AGENT_RECOVERABLE", false, &value)
+        .IgnoreError();
+    return value;
+  }();
+  if (recoverable || recoverable_from_env) {
     LOG(WARNING)
         << "Using experimental recoverable task feature. The default shutdown "
            "barrier will only block non-recoverable tasks. If a synchronized "
--- a/third_party/xla/xla/tsl/distributed_runtime/coordination/BUILD
+++ b/third_party/xla/xla/tsl/distributed_runtime/coordination/BUILD
@@ -137,12 +137,12 @@
         "//xla/tsl/lib/monitoring:gauge",
         "//xla/tsl/platform:env",
         "//xla/tsl/platform:status",
+        "//xla/tsl/util:env_var",
         "//xla/tsl/protobuf:coordination_config_proto_cc",
         "//xla/tsl/protobuf:coordination_service_proto_cc",
         "@com_google_absl//absl/base:core_headers",
         "@com_google_absl//absl/container:flat_hash_map",
         "@com_google_absl//absl/container:flat_hash_set",
-        "@com_google_absl//absl/flags:flag",
         "@com_google_absl//absl/functional:any_invocable",
         "@com_google_absl//absl/functional:bind_front",
         "@com_google_absl//absl/log",
